    {
      "block_id": "2605.23244_p15_b1",
      "text": "\u2022 Define the COALA Objective: COALA uses a modified Bradley-Terry model for preference learning. The reward\nfunction is defined as the un-normalized log-likelihood of the convex policy: r(x, y) = \u03b2 log \u03c0(y|x). The specific\nobjective function (LCOALA) is derived by substituting the convex policy into the logistic loss formula. Crucially, this\nobjective function is convex with respect to the weights (\u03b82).\n",
      "bbox": [
        66.9,
        69.32,
        541.44,
        115.91
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        267,
