    {
      "block_id": "2605.23244_p15_b15",
      "text": "DPO\n\u201cresponse\u201d: \u201cGlucose is a simple sugar and a vital compound in the human body. Glucose is primarily\nresponsible for doing the following: 1. Energy Source: Glucose is the main source of energy for cells in the\nbody. It is used by the body\u2019s cells, particularly the brain, muscles, and organs, to produce energy through a\nprocess called cellular respiration. 2. Fuel for the Brain: Glucose is the main fuel for the brain, providing the\nenergy needed for cognitive functions, memory, and mental activity. 3. Storage of Energy: Glucose is stored\nin the body as glycogen in the liver and muscles. It serves\u201d\n",
